\tag{fdip}
\title{Real commutants and actual form choices}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For a real irreducible representation of a finite group,
an invariant positive inner product restricts the commuting
algebra to three possibilities. That classification does not
choose an invariant bilinear form. A rotation plane and the
real quaternion fiber show how the form needed for a
determinant constraint must still be exhibited.}

